Changes: the fp4/fp8 expert formats (code table, uint8 block scales) are
replaced by MLX affine codes of 4 or 8 bits with bf16 scales and biases, 64
weights a group; a weight is code * scale + bias computed in float and
rounded once to bf16, which is what a Metal quantized matmul multiplies by.
The gate/up launch clamps both projections before silu(gate) * up and has no
per-expert gate scale. The launch geometry and the tensor-core main loop are
unchanged. The weighted top-k sum of GLM-5.3 is not taken from mlx-serve.
Each mma.m16n8k16 step starts from a zero accumulator and its result is
added to the running sum with a correctly rounded float add.
